From 9aa08b06b796bee2e566103727d1dd6acf6a6b5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Downstream Patch Queue <downstream@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] Add independent widget statistics feed

An unscanned projection could replace a lease's stored statistics with six null past days
beside a real today. The projection's calendar day came from the collector's own clock, the
day loop dropped recorded rows whose source was no longer detected, and the publisher sent
whatever the next 30-minute slot produced. A widget-only daemon, which has no SSH client to
observe the gap, therefore appeared to lose its seven-day history after a long background
period even though the relay snapshot carried a fresh today.

Publish only scanned windows. A lease keeps its stored payload while the history is missing,
labelled for an earlier day or built for another timezone; the daemon asks the sampler to
re-project at once and to rescan changed files, and the covering correction is published as
soon as it exists without waiting for the routine slot, as one bounded attempt that still
observes Retry-After. Only the first confirmation attempt may store a real today beside
unscanned past days, and it is corrected immediately afterwards. Recorded rows stay facts
when their source is no longer detected, available or enabled, so a past day keeps its known
input/output lower bound and is merely incomplete. The wire object is unchanged.

The mobile reader currently merges tolerantly to support older daemons that store unscanned
windows. That compatibility layer is temporary and is removed once this publisher rule is
deployed, so null past days are not an acceptable long-term output of the collector.
