+
+## Independent Widget statistics feed (unreleased)
+
+Widget statistics are a separate opt-in authorization, not an extension of ActivityKit's eight-hour lease.
+The same effective-UID/executable-digest daemon and existing scan/parser pipeline supply timestamped input/output counts;
+there is no extra Monitor, per-widget scanner, ordinary notification, or indefinite mobile SSH session.
+Negotiation requires outer `version: 1`, `controlVersion: 2`, capability `widget_statistics_v2`,
+`widgetMinPublishIntervalMs: 1800000`, and `widgetMaxLeaseSeconds: 2592000` alongside existing capabilities.
+Unresponsive or incomplete capabilities do not permit a legacy collector fallback.
+
+`widget_subscribe` requires `requestId`, `subscriptionId` (the registered widget ID), opaque publisher
+`lease`, absolute Unix-millisecond `expiresAt`, registered `hostId`/`hostName`, IANA `timezone`, and
+`intervalMs: 1800000`. The expiry must be in the future and at most 30 days away. No relay URL is accepted
+from the command. The only destination is `https://agent-speed.yooztech.com/v1/widget-publish` with
+`Authorization: Bearer <lease>` and body `{ "snapshot": <statistics> }`.
+
+The statistics object has version 2, registered host identity, genuine snapshot `sampledAt`, fixed
+`timezone`, its calendar `usageDate`, `today`, exactly seven ascending `days`, `models`,
+`modelsComplete`, and `historyComplete`. Today contains `input`, `output`, `requests`,
+`costMicroUsd`, `unpricedRequests`, and `complete`; each day adds `date`. The last day equals
+today in every metric. Counts are nullable nonnegative safe integers. Today's input/output are the
+snapshot's known totals regardless of source availability; today is complete unless history is
+partial, and a partial today nulls all three request/cost fields. A past day retains the known
+input/output sum of the rows of participating sources; a recorded row stays a fact after its source
+is no longer detected, available or enabled, because detection decides only today's live counts.
+The day is incomplete when any participating source lacks a row for that day; its request/cost
+fields require complete source coverage and nonpartial matching history. A day without rows is
+unknown, never zero. Known priced cost is not a full bill when requests are unpriced.
+Model rows contain only `model`, `input`, and `output`: the three highest fully known named models
+by total (name breaks ties), followed by one null-model bucket for all remaining and unnamed usage.
+Each bucket component preserves unknowns. Models come from actual current-date history and may lag
+the live counters. `modelsComplete` requires complete today and matching nonpartial history, all
+participating sources covered, all model components known, and both sums matching today. Missing
+counts and dates are null, never fabricated zeros. `historyComplete` requires all seven days complete.
+Cached input and reasoning are already included; do not add them again. Invalid model IDs, unsafe
+integers or a body larger than 64 KiB fail closed.
+
+A null past day may only mean that the scan covered that day and found no records, or that the
+coverage is incomplete (`complete: false`). It must never mean that the history was not ready. The
+publisher therefore compares a projection's `usageDate` and `timezone` with the sample's own
+calendar day before publishing: a missing, stale or differently labelled projection may not replace
+the statistics already stored for a lease. The lease keeps the stored payload, the daemon asks the
+sampler to re-project at once and to rescan changed source files, and the publisher retries well
+below the routine interval. A covering projection is published as soon as it exists, even inside
+the 30-minute window, as one bounded attempt that still observes Retry-After and does not move the
+routine cadence backwards. The only unscanned projection a lease may store is its first
+confirmation attempt, whose real today counts let the 75-second ACK complete; the covering
+correction follows immediately. The mobile client currently performs an additional reader-side
+merge to tolerate older daemons that store unscanned windows. That compatibility layer is temporary
+and is removed once this publisher rule is deployed, so null past days are not an acceptable
+long-term output of the collector.
+
+`widget_subscribe_ack` echoes `version`, `controlVersion`, `requestId`, `subscriptionId`, `hostId`,
+`hostName`, `timezone`, `expiresAt` and Boolean `accepted`, plus a safe `error` on failure. A positive ACK
+requires a genuine valid first statistics POST returning HTTP **200**, within the bounded 75-second
+confirmation window. This confirms Worker storage, not APNs/device delivery. A failed confirmation must
+not leave the mobile app displaying enabled authority; it independently revokes Worker registration and
+sends a best-effort collector unsubscribe. Same-lease retries preserve the publisher and its attempt
+window; a new authorization replaces it with generation fencing and may publish its initial sample
+immediately. The Worker separately enforces its installation-wide push budget across replacements.
+
+`widget_unsubscribe` requires `version: 1`, `controlVersion: 2`, `requestId`, `subscriptionId`, and the
+matching publisher `lease`. Its ACK echoes the request/subscription IDs and `accepted`. An old credential
+cannot revoke a replacement. Confirmed Widget authorization survives ordinary SSH close until explicit
+unsubscribe, replacement or expiry, independently of ActivityKit ending. Only authenticated foreground
+registration can renew it; the daemon and widget fetch cannot. No widget read credential, registration
+credential, App Attest key or Apple provider secret is sent to the collector. Host logout/cgroup policy
+can still kill the daemon; no linger policy or root service is installed.
+
+After the initial attempt, routine publish attempts are at least 30 minutes apart; the covering
+correction above is the one extra attempt and never turns into a retry storm. Latest real
+source/history changes coalesce; unchanged counts still receive a genuine fresh observation/date at
+the next slot.
+Publishing uses a separate bounded single-flight HTTPS worker, verifies certificates and hostname,
+disables redirects/environment proxies/netrc, limits connection/DNS to three seconds and total request
+time to 15 seconds, and bounds response bytes. No credential appears in argv, environment, URL or logs.
+401/403/410 and other permanent 4xx stop only the matching authorization; 429 observes a later
+Retry-After; transport/5xx retain confirmed authorization until expiry and use the next normal slot,
+not a retry storm. Stale responses cannot resurrect or retire a replacement. Worker storage and
+WidgetKit `widgets` push remain separate: HTTP 200 must preserve newly stored data even when APNs fails.
+
+This is an unpublished source/queue feature. Production ELF and fixed-loopback TLS test ELF are separate;
+only the former may be delivered as a collector asset. Local process/TLS checks do not validate App Attest,
+WidgetKit entitlement/signing, APNs acceptance or actual iPhone timeline delivery.
+
