+## 9. Independent opt-in Widget statistics relay (unreleased)
+
+Foreground mobile consent may separately authorize the shared remote collector to POST a limited
+statistics projection to `https://agent-speed.yooztech.com/v1/widget-publish`. This is not ActivityKit
+authority: its scoped opaque publisher lease lasts at most 30 days, cannot be renewed by the daemon,
+and survives SSH close only within that authorization. Disable/forget/host changes revoke the Worker
+registration independently and attempt an exact lease-scoped collector unsubscribe. Ending a Live
+Activity does not revoke a separately authorized Widget feed. With no SSH clients or either kind of
+valid authorization, the daemon still exits after its bounded idle period.
+
+The version 2 body contains registered host identity, actual observation time/date/IANA timezone,
+today and seven calendar days of input, output, requests, known priced micro-USD and unpriced requests,
+and up to three named models plus a null-model remainder from actual current-date history. Coverage and
+model completeness are explicit; missing values remain null, not zero. Cost is not a complete bill when
+unpriced requests exist. The widget projection contains no source breakdown, transcript, raw log,
+command, path, SSH credential, full history database or Apple provider secret. It is at most 64 KiB.
+Fixed endpoint TLS verifies certificates/hostname, prohibits redirects/proxies/netrc, and bounds
+connection/DNS to three seconds and the complete request to 15 seconds. Initial storage may occur
+immediately; later same-authorization routine attempts occur no more frequently than every 30
+minutes, with a later Retry-After respected. A past day is null only when the scan covered that day
+and found no records; a projection whose history is missing, stale or labelled for another calendar
+day never replaces the stored one, and the covering correction is published as soon as it exists as
+one bounded attempt. Only the first confirmation attempt may carry real today counts beside
+unscanned past days, and it is corrected immediately afterwards. There is no per-second Widget push
+or permanently authorized feed.
+
+HTTP 200 acknowledges storage only; a failed Apple push must not erase the stored projection. The Worker
+owns its independent installation-wide 30-minute push budget across host/token/lease replacements.
+WidgetKit push only invalidates a widget timeline; no ordinary notification, alert, sound or
+push-to-start is introduced. Narrow read/token-update credentials stay on the mobile/extension side,
+not the target host. Read access does not renew publisher authority, and removing widgets may stop
+pushes while a separately consented publisher lease continues storing bounded statistics until expiry.
+Local development checks and an unpublished ELF are not proof of production deployment or Apple delivery.
+
